            <h2>2. The Psychology of Daily Movement</h2>
            <p>You shouldn't wait until you "have more free time" to start exercising; movement is a priority that builds energy and longevity, regardless of your busy schedule. Small, consistent activities do wonders. Taking a 15-minute walk after meals, using standing desks, or doing a quick morning stretch routine compounds over time to deliver massive cardiovascular benefits. Your goal isn't just weight loss; it's protecting your joints and heart as you age.</p>

