            <h2>4. Mastering Sleep and Stress Management</h2>
            <p>You can eat perfectly and exercise daily, but unmanaged stress and sleep deprivation will destroy your progress. Focus on eliminating late-night screen time and establish a solid sleep hygiene routine. Aim for 7-9 hours of high-quality sleep every night to allow your muscles to repair and your brain to consolidate memories and flush out toxins. A dark, cold room is your best defense against insomnia.</p>

