            <h2>6. Posture and Ergonomic Health</h2>
            <p>Tech neck and lower back pain have become modern epidemics. If you spend 8 hours a day staring at a laptop or smartphone, your spine is paying the price. Investing in an ergonomic chair, positioning your monitor at eye level, and practicing "chin tucks" can save you thousands of dollars in physical therapy down the road. Remember, poor posture doesn't just look bad; it restricts your lung capacity and elevates stress hormones.</p>
            
            <h2>7. Gut Health and the Microbiome</h2>
            <p>Science has confirmed that your gut is your second brain. Trillions of bacteria living in your digestive tract dictate everything from your immune system strength to your daily mood. To optimize your microbiome, you must incorporate fermented foods like kimchi, kefir, and kombucha into your diet, while significantly reducing refined sugars that feed harmful bacteria.</p>

