            <h2>8. The Importance of Flexibility and Mobility</h2>
            <p>Strength training is crucial, but without mobility, you are just building stiff muscles. Incorporating dynamic stretching, yoga, or Pilates into your weekly routine ensures that your joints move through their full range of motion. Mobility work flushes out lactic acid, accelerates muscle recovery, and ensures that you can comfortably perform daily tasks well into your older years.</p>

            <h2>9. Intermittent Fasting Demystified</h2>
            <p>Fasting is not a diet; it's an eating schedule. Giving your digestive system a break for 14-16 hours a day allows your body to enter a state of "autophagy," where it cleans out damaged cells and regenerates new ones. Fasting also naturally lowers insulin levels, making it easier for your body to tap into stored fat for energy instead of relying on a constant stream of glucose.</p>
            
