            <h2>12. Breathing Techniques for Nervous System Regulation</h2>
            <p>When you are stressed, your breathing becomes shallow and rapid, keeping your body in a "fight or flight" state. Techniques like Box Breathing (inhale 4s, hold 4s, exhale 4s, hold 4s) or the 4-7-8 method can instantly activate your parasympathetic nervous system. Taking just two minutes a day to consciously breathe can dramatically lower anxiety and improve mental clarity.</p>

            <h2>13. Creating a Toxin-Free Home Environment</h2>
            <p>The air quality inside your home is often worse than the air outside. Transitioning to non-toxic cleaning supplies, using glass containers instead of cheap plastics, and investing in a HEPA air purifier can significantly reduce the chemical load on your liver. Small changes in your environment lead to massive improvements in your long-term cellular health.</p>

